-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",322,{
[10273]="70008751\n1\tTalk to Chieftain Durulkum at Dâr-gazag\tSeek out Chieftain Durulkum at Dâr-gazag, along the ridge south of Gramsfoot. Soldier Faltúrz ordered you to find your way to Chieftain Durulkum at Dâr-gazag.\n",
[10274]="70053E33\n1\tScout Banám Lugaun\tBanám Lugaun can be found in Rath Dúath. You should scout Banám Lugaun.\n2\tTalk to Anborn\tAnborn can be found at Estolad Lân in Rath Dúath. You should talk to Anborn at Estolad Lân.\n",
[10275]="70008768\n1\tTalk to Soldier Gazlup at Lugazag\tIf the tower has not been taken by the enemy, you should find Soldier Gazlup at Lugazag, south and east of Gramsfoot, in the greener sections of the Steps of Gram. Soldier Nartul directed you to speak with Soldier Gazlup at Lugazag.\n",
[10276]="700304A2\n1\tReport to Guthferth, Sergeant at North-torr\tNorth-torr is a fort north of Floodwend, and is the last defence standing in the way of the Easterlings assaulting Floodwend directly. You should find North-torr and speak with Guthferth, the sergeant of that outpost.\n",
[10277]="7003045A\n1\tFind Sergeant Tidlac at Twickenburg\tThe fort of Twickenburg is north of Floodwend along the main road between Harwick and Floodwend. You should seek the sergeant in charge of Twickenburg to see how they fare.\n",
[10278]="7001750C\n1\tDeliver the sample to Foreman Indrith at the Great Wheel\030Collect Water-sample\tForeman Indrith is at the Great Wheel to the east of the Vile Maw. Kaldi handed the sample back to you and sent you to speak with Indrith about what is wrong with the water and to find out what should be done at the Vile Maw.\n2\tTalk to Kaldi at the Vile Maw\tKaldi is at his camp outside the Vile Maw, west of the Great Wheel. Foreman Indrith did not like what he saw within the water and sent you back to Kaldi with a special message.\n",
[10279]="7001E818\n1\tDeliver the yew fishing-rod to Léoflac\030Collect a yew fishing-rod for the Eglain (quantity: see journal)\tCraft and deliver the fishing-rod to Léoflac at the Ost Guruth encampment. The Eglain have asked that fishing-rods be crafted and delivered to assist them in their efforts to survive in the harsh climate of the Lone-lands.\n",
[10280]="7001E81C\n1\tDeliver the Bow Chant: Minor Foe-finder to Léoflac\030Collect Bow Chants: Minor Foe-finder (total: 8)\tCraft eight copies of Bow Chant: Minor Foe-finder and deliver them to Léoflac at the Eglan-encampment at Ost Guruth. The Eglain, in an effort to better prepare their provisioners for the dangers posed by the spiders of the Lone-lands, request the creation and collection of foe-finder bow-chants.\n",
[10281]="7001E822\n1\tDeliver the Gondorian throwing hatchets to Léoflac\030Collect Gondorian throwing hatchets (total: 3)\tCraft three Gondorian throwing hatchets and deliver them to Léoflac at the Eglan-encampment at Ost Guruth. Gondorian throwing hatchets will be used to assist the Eglan-provisioners in providing enough food for the entirety of their people.\n",
[10282]="7001E819\n1\tDeliver the hearty onion soup to Léoflac\030Collect servings of hearty onion soup (total: 2)\tCraft two servings of hearty onion soup and deliver them to Léoflac at the Eglan-encampment at Ost Guruth. The Eglain, in an effort to stave off the spread of disease, have asked for cooks to make them hearty onion soup.\n",
[10283]="7001E81F\n1\tDeliver the heavy cotton cloak to Léoflac\030Collect a heavy cotton cloak (quantity: see journal)\tCraft a heavy cotton cloak and deliver it to Léoflac at the Eglan-encampment at Ost Guruth. To restore their cloth trade, the Eglain require a good number of heavy cotton cloaks.\n",
[10284]="7001E81E\n1\tDeliver the ruby ring of willpower to Léoflac\030Collect a ruby ring of willpower\tCraft a ruby ring of willpower and deliver it to Léoflac at the Eglan-encampment at Ost Guruth. Defending their people from the spiders of the Lone-lands is one goal of the Eglain. If they can find crafters able to create ruby rings of willpower, they believe that they can protect a good number of their people.\n",
[10285]="7001E816\n1\tDeliver the tools of the expert explorer to Léoflac\030Collect tools of the expert explorer for the Eglain (quantity: see journal)\tCraft and deliver tools of the expert explorer to Léoflac at the Ost Guruth encampment. The Eglain have asked that tools of the expert explorer be crafted and delivered to assist them in their efforts to survive in the harsh climate of the lone-lands.\n",
[10286]="700032BC\n1\tCollect Dora's chickens (total: 3)\tDora's chickens are at her farm north of Waymeet, at the end of the first stone path on the right off the main road. You went to Waymeet to help Dora Brownlock at the behest of Peony Grubb. Dora has in turn asked you to rescue her chickens from her farm, which has been overrun by the wolves.\n2\tBring chickens to Dora Brownlock\tDora Brownlock is at the centre of Waymeet. Dora Brownlock will be pleased to have her chickens returned to her, safe from the threat of the wolves prowling about her farm. You should return to her at once.\n",
[10287]="70048C6B\n1\tFind Viznak\tViznak the goblin is being held somewhere in the infected Orc village of Faltor Gâm. You should find Viznak.\n2\tDefeat Ulúrilz\tViznak has been found in the Orc village of Faltor Gâm, tied to an altar. You should rescue Viznak by defeating Ulúrilz!\n3\tHelp Viznak\tViznak has been found in the Orc village of Faltor Gâm, tied to an altar. You should help Viznak escape the altar.\n4\tTalk to Viznak\tViznak is free and has returned to his hideout. You should talk to Viznak.\n",
[10288]="7006D1C7\n1\tDefeat Ordâkhai soldiers (total: 12)\tDefeat the Ordâkhai bullying the people of Gha Nêkha.\n2\tDefeat Upóha\tYou have reclaimed Gha Nêkha for the people. The Ordâkhai captain has come forth to challenge you. You should answer his challenge.\n",
[10289]="70066EA2\n1\tUpokhir has asked you to rescue some fellow dissenters in Pahor Boha. Pahor Boha can be found in the south-east of Pinnath Gelin.\t\n2\tTalk to Upokhir\tYou to have rescued the imprisoned warriors within Pahor Boha and should report your success. Talk to Upokhir in Ost Arndir.\n",
[10290]="7006138D\n1\tDefeat half-orcs at Tham Amothir (total: 10)\tGildor needs you to cause a distraction so that he can rescue Periwinkle. You should defeat half-orcs at Tham Amothir.\n2\tReturn to Gildor outside of Tham Amothir\tYou have caused enough of a distraction. You should return to Gildor outside of Tham Amothir.\n3\tTalk to Periwinkle\tThanks to your help, Gildor has successfully rescued Periwinkle from Tham Amothir. Periwinkle seems to have something she wants to show you.\n4\tTalk to Gildor\tGildor has something to add.\n",
[10291]="7006E4C9\n1\tDefeat Dourhands (total: 12)\030Collect treasure-boxes (total: 6)\tThe Dourhands control the port-city of Kheledûl, where Avorthal will soon be taken aboard a ship destined northward. This Dourhand stronghold is also where boxes of treasure stolen from the Longbeards by the Dourhands are stored.\n2\tLocate the Irestone\tYou have collected the treasure-boxes and eliminated many of Kheledûl's Dourhand occupants. Now you must get to the Irestone, the ship preparing to take Avorthal to an unknown port in the north.\n3\tFree Avorthal\tAvorthal is on the deck of the Irestone, still docked at Kheledûl. You should free Avorthal.\n4\tDefend Avorthal\tAvorthal is being held on the Irestone, the ship docked at the port-city of Kheledûl. Unless you free him tonight, the Irestone will carry Avorthal far from rescue and doom Ered Luin to war between dwarves and Elves.\n",
[10292]="700209A0\n1\tTalk to Corunir\tCorunir is waiting to speak with you outside Norbar within the depths of Nûrz Ghâshu.\n2\tMake your way to Norbar\tGolodir is within Norbar. You must reach him as quickly as possible.\n3\tDestroy Torech Lach\tAn ancient fumerole, Torech Lach, has erupted and is blocking your path forward. It must be dealt with so you can proceed.\n4\tMake your way to Norbar\tGolodir is within Norbar. You must reach him with haste.\n5\tDestroy Torech Naur\tAn ancient fumerole, Torech Naur, has erupted and is blocking your path forward. It must be dealt with so you can proceed.\n6\tMake your way to Norbar\tGolodir is within Norbar. You must reach him with haste.\n7\tDestroy Torech Ruin\tAn ancient fumerole, Torech Ruin, has erupted and is blocking your path forward. It must be dealt with so you can proceed.\n8\tTalk to Corunir in Norbar\tCorunir has ventured into Norbar. Follow him and speak with him about rescuing Golodir.\n9\tPacify Golodir\tGolodir has been driven mad by some force within Nûrz Ghâshu and must be subdued. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n10\tTalk to Corunir\tCorunir is troubled by his friend's actions. Speak with him within Norbar\n11\tDefeat Erebún\tErebún, an ancient Rogmul, has imposed its will upon Golodir's mind. If he is defeated, perhaps Golodir's grief-borne madness will dissipate. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n12\tErebún has been defeated, and Golodir's mind is clear once more. You should speak now with him. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\t\n",
[10293]="70029FC7\n1\tComplete 'Rescue in Nûrz Ghâshu' in a raid group\tGolodir has ventured deep within Nûrz Gâshu, and his close friend Corunir is desperate to save him.\n",
[10294]="70062BBC\n1\tTalk to Deryn atop a hill north-west of Bloodhollow\tDeryn is going to lead the scout group to the north-west. Talk to Deryn atop a hill to the north-west.\n2\tComplete 'Rescue Eluna: Scout-warrior Sortie'\030Complete 'Rescue Eluna: Formidable Foe'\tMarget and Murig are following Eluna's trail. Help Marget and Murig.\n3\tComplete 'Rescue Eluna: One Last Diversion'\tThe way is clear and you should return to Lhan Garan\n",
[10295]="70062BDA\n1\tDefeat a Draig-lûth scout-warrior\tA scout-warrior leads the Draig-lûth search party. Defeat the Draig-lûth scout-warrior.\n2\tTalk to Marget\tYou have defeated a Draig-lûth scout-warrior. Return to Marget.\n",
[10296]="70062BFB\n1\tLure and defeat a Draig-lûth warrior\tMarget would have you lure Dragon-clan warriors south to the base of the hills. Marget has asked you to use her horn to draw Dragon-clan warriors away from the river.\n2\tLure and defeat the second Draig-lûth warrior\tUse the Dunlending horn to draw enemies away from Eluna and her scout-warriors. Defeat Dragon Clan warriors.\n3\tTalk to Eluna\tEluna and her students should have returned to Lhan Garan by now. Talk to Eluna.\n",
[10297]="70062BC1\n1\tDefeat Draig-lûth warriors (total: 8)\tA group of Draig-lûth warriors is searching for Murig and Eluna. Defeat Draig-lûth warriors.\n2\tTalk to Marget\tYou have stirred up plenty of trouble for the Draig-lûth pursuers. Return to Marget.\n",
[10298]="70008280\n1\tEscort Lagorlam to safety\tLagorlam was injured while visiting his vengeance on the trolls. With his anger sated he has offered to leave Taur Gonwaith with you.\n2\tTalk to Thaliollang\tThaliollang is at Lin Giliath, north-west of Taur Gonwaith. Thaliollang will be pleased to hear that you rescued Lagorlam from the forest of Taur Gonwaith.\n",
[10299]="70040005\n1\tFree swan-knights (total: 2)\tThe swan-knights must be rescued.\n",
[10300]="70062081\n1\tRescue Tomur\030Rescue Cledd\030Rescue Tom\030Rescue Arwel\tEdrud Scurloc has asked you to rescue her husband and sons, who went to the Hove farm to fight goblins. The Hove farm is in north-eastern Cardolan.\n2\tReturn to Edrud\tYou have managed to free all of the Scurloc men. You should return to Edrud and let her know they're all safe. Edrud is at the Scurloc farmstead, in north-eastern Cardolan.\n",
[10301]="700700C3\n1\tRecover Corbo's vegetables (total: 12)\tCorbo has asked you to recover some of his vegetables should you happen to find yourself in the shrew-tunnel located south-east of the Staddle village centre in Bree-land.\n2\tReturn the vegetables to Corbo Tunnelly\tYou have rescued a dozen of Corbo's stolen vegetables from the shrew-tunnel beneath Staddle's farmland. You should return them to him at the Staddle village centre in Bree-land.\n",
[10302]="7004429D\n1\tTear down Withered Tree posters in the lower Circles (total: 6)\030Try to inspire despairing citizens in the lower Circles (total: 4)\tParchments posted by the Withered Tree and despairing citizens who read their messages can be found throughout the First and Second Circles of the city. Echadon, the Captain of the Garrison, has asked you to help raise the morale of the people of Minas Tirith in any way you can.\n2\tTalk to Echadon at the south end of the Second Circle\tEchadon is in the Second Circle of the city. You have sought to raise the spirits of people in the lower Circles of the city.\n3\tFind the group of unhappy guards Echadon mentioned, at the north end of the Second Circle\tEchadon is concerned about the morale of a group of his men on the north end of the Second Circle of the city. A feeling of hopelessness has begun to spread throughout the city, and it has affected not just the common folk, but the men of the garrison as well.\n4\tTalk to Celonor at the north end of the Second Circle\tCelonor looks especially worried and downcast.\n5\tCelonor and other men of the garrison are at the north end of the Second Circle, and need tales of courage to inspire them.\t\n6\tCelonor and other men of the garrison are at the north end of the Second Circle, and need tales of courage to inspire them.\t\n7\tTalk to Echadon at the south end of the Second Circle\tEchadon is at the south end of the Second Circle of the city. You have raised the spirits of Celonor and the other men of the garrison.\n",
[10303]="70067F4E\n1\tFind Ayaluk at his home and speak with him\tNûrut asked you to check in on Ayaluk and see if he is well and if he is satisfied with the outcome of the investigation and efforts to expose the overseer's crimes.\n",
[10304]="7002F98E\n1\tThe láthbear menace resides within the wooded areas east of Faldham. Inhere believes that sounding the Rohirrim horn within the clearings among the trees will frighten the láthbears into retreating.\t\n2\tTalk to Inhere about the unyielding láthbears\tInhere awaits at the northern edge of the trees, east of Faldham. Inhere must be informed that the láthbears have not recoiled at the sounds of the Rohirrim horn.\n",
})
